{
  "bridge_text": "刚才那棵大树在寒风中静静守望，现在莉娜已经穿过霜冻的田野，站在了树下。让我们听听接下来发生了什么。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "莉娜裹紧了红色的羊毛大衣，那棵大树就在她眼前，像是一位沉默的守望者，静静地等待着她的到来。每当冬夜，树干里总会传出低沉的嗡嗡声，大人们总说离它远点，但她此刻只想知道那未完的故事究竟藏着什么秘密。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The secret of Mosk's grumpiness hides in the shadows of the tree, waiting for us to discover it. We return now to the steps where Lina stands before the fox.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood firm, her eyes meeting the fox's gaze as she refused to leave the mystery of the humming behind. Mosk sighed, the sound rustling through his fur like autumn wind, and he finally gestured toward the dark, winding path that dipped deeper into the trunk."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the name Mosk firmly tucked away in our memory, we watch as he considers the girl and the small, firm gift she offers him on the step.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a clawed finger toward the exit, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set the fruit on the wooden step between them, offering it as a peace token for the trouble of her visit. The old fox stared at the bright red skin for a long time, his nose twitching. Finally, he stood up, straightened his patched green vest, and stepped onto the first stair downward without saying a word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Down in the depths of the tree, the humming resolved into a quiet, pulsing song. A firefly as large as a robin lay upon a bed of soft moss, her golden glow flickering and dim. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had been his dearest friend, but he had failed to bring her medicine one winter long ago. He had been guarding this hollow ever since, too ashamed to face the light he let fade."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While Lina believes a kind heart is a stronger key than any trick, the fox remains uncertain. She leaves the apple behind, watching as he finally begins his descent.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Lina watched him closely, wondering if the small gift could truly bridge the gap between them. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his gaze heavy with old memories. Finally, he stood up, pulled his vest tight, and stepped onto the first stair without a word, leading the way into the deep."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Just as that soft, mossy blanket cradled the firefly, the gentle hum of the hollow tree seemed to wrap around them, waiting for what would happen next.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming was a quiet song, and a firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of moss—that soft, velvet-green carpet that cushions the earth. Her glow was almost out. Mosk's whiskers trembled as he looked at her. She had been his friend once, he whispered, and one winter long ago he had failed to bring her medicine in time. He had been guarding the tree ever since, far too ashamed to face her."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk watching her closely from the top of those winding stairs, Lina stood her ground, waiting to see if the fox would let her pass into the hollow.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a curl of stairs spiraled downward into the dark. At the very top step sat an old grey fox named Mosk, wearing a vest of patched green cloth that looked as if it had seen many seasons. His voice sounded like dry leaves skittering on stone as he told her that the tree was not for visitors, urging her to go home and forget the humming. But Lina shook her head, insisting she could not forget a sound she had not yet truly heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the apple left behind on the wooden step, Mosk led the way down into the dark, his footsteps echoing softly against the hollow trunk.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. He looked back just once, his eyes reflecting the dim light of the passage, before vanishing into the shadows of the tree's deep, winding heart."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While we wonder if the firefly's light can be mended, the mossy room grows still as Mosk waits for a sign. His past regret hangs heavy in the air, but Lina is here to help.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Mosk's whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He had been her friend once, he whispered, and one winter long ago he had failed to bring her medicine in time. He had been guarding the tree ever since, ashamed to face her, watching her light fade while he hid in the shadows of his own regret."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers. The queen's glow steadied, and the humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before—and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
